      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "Loans sized to project need; recent closings: $1,500,000 predevelopment for Gateway Tower, San Jose (220 units, 30% to 70% AMI, The Core Companies, 2026); $2,000,000 predevelopment for 69th Street Apartments, Sacramento (129 units, 30% to 60% AMI, CRP Affordable Housing, third Sacramento loan since expansion); acquisition loans up to about $9.9 million in Santa Cruz County (2025). Housing Trust reports $785 million invested since 2000. Capitalized by the TECH Fund (Cisco, Packard Foundation, Google, Grove Foundation, Sobrato Family Foundation, LinkedIn, NetApp, Pure Storage, Jewish Community Federation) and the Affordable Housing Growth Fund and 2015 Loan Pool (Avidbank, Beneficial State Bank, Bridge Bank, East West Bank, First Bank, Fremont Bank, Heritage Bank of Commerce, Manufacturers Bank, Presidio Bank, Silicon Valley Bank, Tech CU).",
